          "source_text_sha256": "4442eae8d555c906e6248155b0f3274ed715244ae7a9a1a232af5734c23f6ecb",
          "start_ms": null,
          "status": "machine-unreviewed",
          "text": "Description: On Sunday, September 22, 2013, at 6:45 PM, several people in cars were intrigued by a sight in the sky they couldn't explain. The witness, in a car, described a silver spherical shape transforming into a bright white elongated shape, apparently stationary, then duplicating and disappearing. The radar plot (see diagram) clearly shows a high-altitude plane (black trace) as described by the witness, and also, at low altitude (thus without a trail), a plane moving away from the witness (red trace). The plane, moving away from the witness almost in the line of sight, appeared stationary. When the plane changed direction at 6:50 PM (see top right of the diagram, left turn from 6:48 PM to 51), the reflection changed and disappeared, suggesting the object itself had vanished. (Note: the times indicated along the plane traces are universal time). The witness's first intuition: a reflection of the sun on an airplane ultimately proved to be the correct explanation. The GEIPAN classifies this case as \"A\": perfectly explained by the reflection of the sun on an airplane.",
          "translation_text_sha256": "18fa75e310e32b62d264751dacc95e082d06e844d63cd844a7eb9b6e118d5bde"
        }
